ue way to do  this is to have the user preview their  password by hovering over the actual  button itself as opposed to clicking on  it we can do that by listening to the  mouse enter event and then we'll pass an  anonymous function here that simply  toggles the show password property to  true and then on Mouse leave will toggle  the show password value back to false  then inside the actual button content  will use a ternary operator here to show  a different emoji based on the state of  show password in the final magic to  convert this from a password field to a  text field is to go up here to the input  type and where we have a static string  value for password we'll use a dynamic  ternary that changes it from password to  text based on the state of the  application and now at this point you  should be able to preview the password  value by simply hovering over the emoji  like I'm gonna go ahead and wrap things  up there if you want to see more svelte  content or have more project ideas make  sure to let me know in the comments and  if you want access to more advanced  content consider becoming a pro member  at fire ship IO thanks for watching and  I will see you in the next one  [Music]

